WEBVTT

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.230
Florence at the beginning of the 16th century--

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.730
At the time, most pigments for paints
were procured at apothecaries

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.480
and then mixed at individual workshops.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.190
Oh, you're Arte from Leo's place.
What's the matter?

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.150
You're not as cheerful as usual.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.320
Really?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.820
I can't, I can't. The marketplace
is a nightmare for me today.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.690
I wonder why Leo fasts on Fridays...

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.010
"Inescapable Bond"

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.280
What's with that attitude?!

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:51.110
I'm telling you that I'm giving you work!
Aren't you grateful?!

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.110
Anyway, do it like the order says!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.980
That's all the business I have with you.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:08.230
I've never seen him before.
Was he here about a commission?

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.400
He's a customer I've known for a long time.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.940
Apparently, he's been visiting
foreign countries recently,

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.860
so I haven't seen him in a while.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.570
Oh? Then he's an important customer.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.570
No.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.980
We just have an inescapable bond.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:24.650
Take a look at this.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.110
O-Okay...

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.690
Is this the order form? What about it...?

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.820
Huh?! That's a lot of money!

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.730
Um, is there a zero in the
wrong place in the price?!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.820
That's not the problem.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.320
Huh?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.440
He's asking for a lot of expensive
gold and blue paints...

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:46.030
The subject is complicated, too,
and there are multiple people in the layout...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.570
What's with all this? We won't make any profit!

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:52.030
Anyway, I can't take this job as it is.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.190
I have to go negotiate.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:57.070
It's so annoying I could die...

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.530
Sorry, my real feelings slipped out
before I could stop them.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.320
Even though he usually
never scowls about work...

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.900
It's my first time seeing Leo like this.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.780
Um... Would you like me to go in your place?

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:13.690
Huh?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.280
I was just thinking that in order
to work toward the future,

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:21.690
I should try doing some harder work
like negotiating with the clients and stuff.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.320
Um...

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:28.150
'Cause in order to become independent,
I'll have to be able to do things like that.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.650
B-Besides, since I grew up as a noble,

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:36.480
I'm used to negotiating with
important people and stuff...

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.780
You're just saying that because you can
tell I don't want to do it, right?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.480
Don't force yourself.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.780
You're right. It won't do any good
if someone like me butts in, huh?

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:53.530
But it's possible that even that old man
would be nicer if he's talking to a girl.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:55.530
I'll leave it to you.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.650
I'm counting on you, Arte.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.860
I thought it was around here...

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.820
What is this? The atmosphere feels
different from the area we live in.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:15.150
It's like this whole district
is one big workshop.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.780
Here, huh?

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.400
Apparently, he's a wealthy merchant
who oversees this whole area.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.070
Please wait here.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.400
What's with this room...?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.230
Wow...

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:47.440
There are so many paintings... Paintings...

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.070
Huh? Are you Mr. Ubertino, sir?

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.610
Please excuse me. Um, I'm...

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:09.610
I heard that Leo's apprentice
had come. Is that you, girl?

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:16.030
I didn't know he'd taken on
an apprentice. And a girl, at that...

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:20.110
You're not pretending to be something
you're not, are you, girl?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.690
Mr. Ubertino, I would never
do anything of the sort.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.320
I am truly Leo's apprentice.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:36.940
I see. Very well. I will listen
to what you have to say.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.860
Come with me.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.610
This is my study. Come in.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.360
Excuse me.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.230
Huh? There's nothing in the study...

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.900
Now, what did you come
here for, Leo's apprentice?

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.230
Oh, right!

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:01.400
Actually, there were some things
we wanted to revise in the order...

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.030
Oh?

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:09.400
In other words, what? Do you have
complaints about my order?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.980
He's scary...

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.940
But I can't lose to him here.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:18.780
I'll do my best... and make
these negotiations a success!

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.230
I'm sorry. I couldn't do it.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.530
I'm not surprised...

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.730
Don't worry about it.
That old man's a tough opponent.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:30.860
Leave the rest to me.
You can go back to your own work.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:35.110
Um, Leo... Will you let me try one more time?

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.190
Hm?

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:42.440
I said I'd do it, and you even gave me
the chance, so it's really frustrating.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:50.190
I know I'm being selfish, but if you'll let me,
I'd like to try again with more preparation.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.730
It's like you to want to do it
because you're frustrated.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:53.940
Huh?

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:59.360
Arte, your goal is to become an
independent artisan in the future, right?

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:00.280
Yes, sir.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:03.980
An artisan's job isn't just
to paint a good painting.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:10.480
In the future, you will also need to be able
to get enough work and make enough profit.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.480
This is good timing.
Keep trying until you're satisfied.

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:17.280
Thank you very much! I'll do my best!

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.190
But what strategy should
I use to deal with this?

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.480
Hm...

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.940
Oh!

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.730
Oh, Arte! I'm so happy you came to see me!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.480
What's the matter?

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.690
I have a favor to ask of you, Veronica!

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:40.030
Negotiate? With Ubertino?

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:41.610
Do you know him?

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:45.940
Of course. Because of my work,
I know all the important people in town.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.570
Let's see...

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.070
He started with buying and selling woolen goods,

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.440
and in his lifetime,
he amassed that vast fortune.

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.570
He's a pretty big deal.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.530
H-He's that amazing?

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:03.070
Well? What would you like me to do?

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:06.650
I thought that because of your work,

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:11.980
you'd know how to make a conversation
turn to your advantage...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.480
Will you... teach me how to do that?

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:22.610
I never thought I'd be
teaching anybody anything!

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.400
Huh?

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.400
Sure.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:29.820
I can't turn down a request
like that from a friend.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.730
I'll show you the results of my week!

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:39.650
You again, girl? What do you want now?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:43.190
If it's nothing important,
then hurry up and go home.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:48.610
Mr. Ubertino, please forgive me for
coming to negotiate the other day

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.360
before I collected my thoughts properly.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.480
I have come today to speak with you
about how we can create a work

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.610
that will be even more pleasing to you.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.360
Hm... Very well. I'll listen.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.360
Thank you very much.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:07.480
Let's see. First, stand up straight
and tuck in your chin.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:12.780
Keep a posture full of confidence,
and don't stop smiling.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:16.150
Move slowly and speak slowly.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:20.980
Arte, do you feel grateful just being
able to make money doing art?

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:21.980
Huh?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:25.780
Like, even if you don't earn much, you're just
happy being able to paint for a living?

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.690
You can't think like that.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.730
Huh?!

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:34.940
Then it's like you're saying that you can't
make anything worth more than that.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:38.280
It's rude to make people pay
for something like that.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.940
Have confidence that you can make
something worth a large sum.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:46.900
In order to do that, use all the weapons
you have in your arsenal,

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:50.980
including the fact that you are
a woman and from a noble family.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:54.150
About this order form we
received the other day--

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:58.570
The compensation is not enough to create
a work with the materials specified here.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:02.980
We talked about this the other day, didn't we?
How many times do I have to explain?

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:08.190
I know the market price for paints.
This price for these materials is appropriate.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:12.980
No, Mr. Ubertino, this is nowhere <i>near</i> enough.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:19.280
What? Then what, are you trying to
unfairly cheat a customer out of money?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.110
Even if something is made
from expensive materials,

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.820
without the skill of an artisan,

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.860
you won't be able to create
something worth their price.

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:38.730
At our workshop, my master is skilled enough
to create something worth that price.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:41.730
In addition, I am from a noble family.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:44.900
Huh? Noble? What about it?

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.190
Are you saying I should pay more
because you're a noble?

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:52.070
No. I would like you to take a look at this.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.030
Drawings of lace?

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:59.070
Oh? These are very elaborate...

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.940
These were studies I drew.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.110
What?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:06.190
As befitting of a girl from a noble family,
I studied many things.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:09.940
Do you think there are any painters in
Florence who have learned to crochet?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.480
I can use those skills in my painting.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:20.230
Mr. Ubertino, I will increase the value
of the painting even more.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:28.150
I'll sign a new contract with you.

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:33.360
But I won't let you get away with giving me
something I'm not satisfied with, girl.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.110
Anyway, what's with that deportment
that doesn't suit you?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.820
Did you learn that from
a prostitute or something?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.860
Anyway, this will cost a lot of money.
So much it'll make you sick.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.360
There's nothing more wasteful
than paintings and decoration.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:50.110
Huh? But in the parlor...

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:53.530
That's to bluff my customers.
They're tools for my work.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:57.730
There's no way I'd order paintings
if it were completely up to me.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:03.570
That's why the parlor was so elaborately
decorated, but this study is so bare.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:08.400
Um, then your own feelings about paintings...

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.530
I'm not interested in them at all.

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:14.230
Even if I look at a painting,
I don't feel moved at all.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:19.280
I just have knowledge of what
kinds of paintings are good.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:22.690
Hm? What, are you shocked?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:26.940
Did you think that only people
who liked art ordered paintings?

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.650
Huh? No, of course not...

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:36.320
I use paintings as gifts to influential people
and donations to the Church to curry favor.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.780
Paintings are not ordered
by people who love art.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:44.110
They're ordered as tools
by people who have money.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.360
Tools...

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.860
I'm sure you'll have a chance to work
with people like me in the future

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.820
who don't understand art.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.820
If you're so surprised by what you just heard,

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:58.480
then you'll be disappointed in your
current line of work one of these days.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.320
Then I couldn't ask for anything more.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:07.030
I'll become an artisan who can
satisfy even people like that.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:15.820
Leo found himself an interesting
apprentice with a competitive spirit.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.980
Can I take that as a compliment...?

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:23.320
At the very least, <i>I</i> like you.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:31.150
Well then... please excuse me.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:32.570
Oh, right!

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:36.900
Um, Mr. Ubertino, I have a favor to ask you.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.400
Is it really something you want
to look at so many times?

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.360
Yes, I wanted to see this again!

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.940
There are so, so many paintings! It's wonderful!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.690
Is it really something to get so excited about?

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:50.690
Yes, it is!

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:54.150
These paintings... These paintings...

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:01.150
The paintings in this room... Leo's touch...

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:05.280
Wait, aren't most of the paintings
in this room Leo's work...?

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:10.570
It appears you like Leo very much,
don't you, Mr. Ubertino?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:16.280
I don't like that man one bit!
We just have an inescapable bond.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.900
Huh?! Is he really angry?

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:23.940
Besides, half the paintings here
were done by his teacher.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.730
What? Leo's teacher?

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.820
N-No way... Leo...

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.900
<i>That</i> Leo... had a childhood?!

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.480
I can't imagine it at all!

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:43.730
I see, I see! It <i>is</i> hard
to imagine Leo as a child!

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:48.150
Um, how long have you and Leo
known each other--?

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.150
What, are you hungry?

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.690
No, this is because we fast on Fridays...

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:57.610
What, Leo's fasting?

00:15:57.610 --> 00:16:00.730
There's no way he's doing that
because of his faith!

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:03.150
He's just being stingy!

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:06.610
He and Leo really don't get along, huh...

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:11.360
Girl, stop by the kitchen on your way back.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.150
Huh?

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:15.650
The negotiations were successful!

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:16.730
What?

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:21.320
Your master and Ubertino knew each other, huh?

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:24.980
That old man talked about
my master? What did he say?

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:27.230
He didn't say much about your master...

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.360
But he did say he never liked <i>you</i> .

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:34.690
I didn't know <i>anything</i> about you, Leo!

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:37.530
I was surprised to hear you had a childhood!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:41.440
What, are you so interested in me?

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.150
I...

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:45.280
I'm really, really interested!

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:51.400
There's no way I <i>wouldn't</i> be interested
in what my master was like as an apprentice!

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:54.780
Besides, we're talking about <i>you</i> here!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:59.610
You have no intention of hiding
that curiosity of yours, huh?

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:02.780
It's actually kind of refreshing.

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:04.400
When I was an apprentice...

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:07.110
...at the very least, I didn't make
careless mistakes like you,

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:11.190
and I wasn't clumsy or noisy like you, either.

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:15.280
But before I joined a workshop,
I was the same as you.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:16.150
Huh?

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:19.190
I went around to different
workshops with my art.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:21.820
Most of them turned me away
at the door, though...

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:25.820
Leo went around to workshops like I did...?

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:27.780
That's unusual.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:32.730
I thought most people's apprenticeships
were arranged by their parents.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.940
It's because I was a beggar.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:38.650
I did my work earnestly,

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:41.690
but I was a troublemaker who didn't
get along with those around me.

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:45.280
Even so, my master didn't throw me out.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.730
He must've been a kind man.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:53.110
He was also strict and coldhearted...

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:03.150
Um, you were a beggar, right?

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.440
Yeah.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:09.820
I'm glad... that I was able to come here,
to apprentice under you.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:15.190
You started off in a more difficult situation
than others and became a master.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:20.320
For me, that means there's
a lot I can learn from you.

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:33.360
You're too cocky, just because you're
a little faster at your work!

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.860
Even though you're a beggar!

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:39.030
I'm just faster because I worked hard!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:41.900
You've been blessed so much more than I have!

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.860
Don't just complain without putting in any work!

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:45.730
Wha--?!

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:48.900
--Stop messing around!
--Bastard!

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:51.820
They're the ones who came at me.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:54.530
You should just ignore them...

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:58.650
Leo, this part isn't good.
I told you before, remember?

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:01.480
Don't make the same mistake over and over.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:08.820
Master doesn't say anything to those guys,
no matter how many mistakes they make.

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.530
I wonder if it's because I used to be a beggar.

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:15.280
That's what I thought at the time,

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.400
but as we continued our training
as apprentice artisans,

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:22.480
the difference between my skills
and theirs became even greater.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:27.030
That was when I finally understood
what my master was thinking.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.530
He wasn't being kind at all.

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:33.690
He had no intention of doing anything
for people who didn't put in the effort.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:39.230
He treated everyone equally
when it came to work.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:50.150
Hm, I see. It does appear
to be worth what I paid.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:52.030
Be that as it may,

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:57.070
all your tools are expensive ones,
and you bought new ones, too, didn't you?

00:19:57.070 --> 00:20:01.940
The tools Father bought me
were probably high quality,

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:04.860
but I've never felt that
the ones here were lacking.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:09.440
Despite that, why are your clothes so shabby?!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:13.980
On top of that, I heard you're
fasting and eating frugally!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:18.980
Oh, I see. His fasting and
wearing shabby clothes

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:23.150
were all because he wanted to save
all his money for his work.

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:27.230
If you have enough money,
then how about using some for yourself?

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:32.070
If you're going to live like this forever,
then what's the point in me being your patron?

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:35.530
Your "Shut up, old man!" aura
is totally leaking out, Leo!

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:40.780
Right, Mr. Ubertino! I'll carry
the painting out to your carriage!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:45.900
I can't believe him! You should tell him, too.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:50.400
To use more money for himself!

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:57.070
Ubertino... Despite everything he said,
is he worried about Leo?

00:20:57.070 --> 00:21:02.440
Hmph. You left behind
a troublesome apprentice...

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:10.150
Mr. Ubertino... Please take care of Leo...

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:14.480
Master and apprentice both cause me trouble...

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:20.280
That annoying job is finally done.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:23.110
I wish he wouldn't commission me anymore.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:26.820
Don't say that, Leo! He's a regular, isn't he?

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.360
The painting this time was
for work, too, wasn't it?

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.570
Every time, he uses so much money for work...

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:35.690
That old man doesn't use any
for himself, you know.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.980
Huh?

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.900
Leo and Ubertino...

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.940
Hm? What is it, all of a sudden?

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.400
It's nothing.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:51.530
I see--the two of them are
worried about each other.

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:56.940
I didn't notice until they said something,
but the two of them could see it already.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:22:00.610
That's amazing. How did they know?

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:07.110
I wonder if there will ever be a day
when I know what Leo's thinking or feeling...

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:10.360
I wonder if we'll be able to look at
the world from the same perspective

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:13.980
if I keep working and getting
a little closer to Leo...

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:19.030
What? You suddenly start laughing,
and then get quiet...

00:22:19.030 --> 00:22:22.610
Hurry up and get back to work, Arte.

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:25.030
Yes, sir!

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:59.450
"Preview"

00:23:56.730 --> 00:24:01.530
If I were a boy, would the people in
the guild recognize me as one of them?

00:24:01.530 --> 00:24:03.400
Arte, you're fine the way you are!

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:06.690
You're right! I'll do my best as I am now!

00:24:04.780 --> 00:24:04.880
"Trade Guild"

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:11.050
"Trade Guild"

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:08.530
Next time, "Trade Guild."

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:11.030
Stop fighting!
